Journey: An adjuster approves a claim within the limit; payout, event and e-mail agree
Id: approve-within-limit
Tags: @backoffice @claims @integration @regression @kafka @email
Role: adjuster
Risk: 5
Requirements: ADJ-1, ADJ-3, PAY-1, EVT-2, NOTIF-2
Variables: claimed=1800, approved=1650.40

# Precondition through the partner API (a code step from the shared library)
Run code "steps/claims.steps.ts#seedClaim" with policyId="POL-H-100231", type="STORM", amount="${claimed}" as seeded
Set variable claimId to seeded.claimId
Get the value of query "SELECT deductible FROM policies WHERE id = 'POL-H-100231'" on claims as excess
Set variable payout to formatNumber(max(0, number(approved) - number(excess)), 2)
Start listening on Kafka topic "larkspur.claims.events" on events as decisions

Log in
Type "${claimId}" into @ClaimDesk.search
Click the "Search" button
  Expect the "Claims queue" table contains "${claimId}"
Click the "Review" link in the row containing "${claimId}"
  Expect the page contains "Review claim ${claimId}"
Expect @ClaimDesk.status has text "In review"
Clear @ClaimDesk.approvedAmount
Type "${approved}" into @ClaimDesk.approvedAmount
Select "Covered in full" from @ClaimDesk.reason
Click @ClaimDesk.approve
  Expect the page contains "Claim ${claimId} approved"
Expect @ClaimDesk.payout has text "${payout}"

Get the first row of query "SELECT status, approved_amount, payout_amount, decision_by, settlement_code FROM claims WHERE id = '${claimId}'" on claims as row
Expect ${row.status} equals "APPROVED"
Expect ${row.approved_amount} == ${approved}
Expect ${row.payout_amount} == ${payout}
Expect ${row.decision_by} equals "dana.okafor"

Wait for a message in decisions where "$.claimId" = "${claimId}" and "$.type" = "claim.approved" within 20 s matching schema "schemas/claim-event.schema.json" as approvedEvent
Expect response approvedEvent "$.payoutAmount" equals "${payout}"
Expect response approvedEvent "$.deductible" equals "${excess}"
Expect response approvedEvent "$.decisionBy" equals "dana.okafor"

Wait for an email to "amelia.hart@mail.larkspur.test" with subject "Claim ${claimId} approved - confirm your settlement" within 20 seconds as offer
Expect ${offer.text} contains "We will pay: ${payout} GBP"
Extract the code from ${offer.text} matching "confirmation code is (\d{6})" as code
Expect ${code} equals "${row.settlement_code}"

Run code "steps/claims.steps.ts#removeClaim" with claimId="${claimId}" as cleanup
